{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is to implement a `solve(case)` function for Toolformer API-call filtering. Let me understand the requirements:\n\n1. For each call: compute gain = `loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by prediction tokens: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. Require both `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return accepted call IDs and per-call diagnostics in original order\n\nThe contracts:\n- `normalized_weights`: normalize by prediction tokens\n- `stronger_counterfactual`: use `loss_without - loss_with` (the gain)\n- `inclusive_threshold`: `\u003e=` not `\u003e`\n- `stable_order`: preserve source order\n\nLet me think about the output format. The description says:\n- \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics\"\n- \"Preserve every source identifier needed to audit the decision\"\n- \"compute aggregate values from the returned primitive decisions\"\n\nSo the return should have:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of call IDs that passed\n- `diagnostics`: list of per-call diagnostic objects (in source order)\n\nPer-call diagnostics should include:\n- `call_id`\n- `gain` (loss_without - loss_with)\n- `normalized_gain` (gain / prediction_tokens)\n- `parseable`\n- `accepted` (bool)\n\nLet me also think about what \"rounded\" means - probably round to some decimal places. Let me use round(..., 8) or something reasonable. Actually, looking at the fixture data, the values have 8 decimal places. I'll round to 8 decimal places.\n\nValidation requirements:\n- Raise ValueError for infeasible/invalid cases\n- Validate every required field before computing\n\nRequired fields in payload:\n- `threshold`: float\n- `calls`: list of call objects\n  - `call_id`: string\n  - `loss_without_call`: float\n  - `loss_with_call`: float\n  - `prediction_tokens`: int (must be \u003e= 1 for normalization)\n  - `parseable`: bool\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    payload = case.get(\"payload\")\n    if payload is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing 'payload' in case\")\n    \n    # Validate threshold\n    if \"threshold\" not in payload:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing 'threshold' in payload\")\n    threshold = payload[\"threshold\"]\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"'threshold' must be numeric\")\n    \n    # Validate calls\n    if \"calls\" not in payload:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing 'calls' in payload\")\n    calls = payload[\"calls\"]\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"'calls' must be a list\")\n    \n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    \n    for i, call in enumerate(calls):\n        # Validate required fields\n        for field in (\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"):\n            if field not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Call at index {i} missing field '{field}'\")\n        \n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        # Validate types\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Call '{call_id}': 'loss_without_call' must be numeric\")\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Call '{call_id}': 'loss_with_call' must be numeric\")\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, int) or isinstance(prediction_tokens, bool):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Call '{call_id}': 'prediction_tokens' must be an integer\")\n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Call '{call_id}': 'prediction_tokens' must be at least 1\")\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Call '{call_id}': 'parseable' must be a boolean\")\n        \n        # Compute gain (stronger counterfactual)\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        \n        # Normalize by prediction tokens\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        # Decision: require parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold (inclusive)\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"gain\": round(gain, 8),\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 8),\n            \"parseable\": parseable,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics,\n        \"total_calls\": len(calls),\n        \"total_accepted\": len(accepted_call_ids)\n    }\n```\n\nLet me verify with the fixture data:\n\nCase fg1-agent-tf-01-a-000:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, norm = 1.56265595/5 = 0.31253119, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, norm = 0.37796304/4 = 0.09449076, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, norm = 0.74550131/6 = 0.12425022, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, norm = 0.7595393/5 = 0.15190786, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, norm = 0.20983801/5 = 0.04196760, parseable=true → NOT accepted (0.042 \u003c 0.05)\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, norm = 0.76393214/4 = 0.19098304, parseable=true → accepted\n\nSo accepted = [call0, call1, call2, call3, call5]\n\nCase fg1-agent-tf-01-a-002:\n- call4: parseable=false → NOT accepted regardless of gain\n\nThis looks correct. The response format requirement says to return a single JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n\nLet me write the final JSON response. I need to be careful about escaping.\n\nThe response format instruction says: return JSON with key \"implementation\" containing Python source. No markdown, no fences.\n\nLet me construct the Python source carefully and then format it as JSON.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import math\\n\\n    payload = case.get(\\\"payload\\\")\\n    if payload is None:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing 'payload' in case\\\")\\n\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in payload:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing 'threshold' in payload\\\")\\n    threshold = payload[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)) or isinstance(threshold, bool):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"'threshold' must be numeric\\\")\\n\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in payload:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing 'calls' in payload\\\")\\n    calls = payload[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"'calls' must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n\\n    for i, call in enumerate(calls):\\n        for field in (\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"):\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Call at index {i} missing required field '{field}'\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)) or isinstance(loss_without, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Call '{call_id}': 'loss_without_call' must be numeric\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)) or isinstance(loss_with, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Call '{call_id}': 'loss_with_call' must be numeric\\\")\\n        if isinstance(prediction_tokens, bool) or not isinstance(prediction_tokens, int):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Call '{call_id}': 'prediction_tokens' must be an integer\\\")\\n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Call '{call_id}': 'prediction_tokens' must be at least 1\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Call '{call_id}': 'parseable' must be a boolean\\\")\\n\\n        # stronger counterfactual: gain = loss without call minus loss with call\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n\\n        # normalize by prediction token count (weighted normalization)\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n\\n        # inclusive threshold: accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"gain\\\": round(gain, 8),\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": round(normalized_gain, 8),\\n            \\\"parseable\\\": parseable,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n    # aggregate values derived from per-call decisions, not recomputed\\n    total_calls = len(calls)\\n    total_accepted = len(accepted_call_ids)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics,\\n        \\\"total_calls\\\": total_calls,\\n        \\\"total_accepted\\\": total_accepted\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01LrovVn5CrUqoTYCUOliPUX","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2054,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":35,"output_tokens":2519,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1691},"service_tier":"standard"}}